## Recommended Pattern: Scoped Service + Interactive Islands

The core challenge is your **static layout can't re-render reactively**. The solution:

### 1. Make reactive parts interactive islands

Even though MainLayout itself is static, you can embed interactive components within it:

```razor
<!-- MainLayout.razor (stays static, no @rendermode) -->
<header>
    <ThemeIndicator @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</header>
@Body
```

### 2. Scoped `ThemeService` (per-circuit state)

Register as `AddScoped<IThemeService, ThemeService>()`. In Interactive Server mode, "scoped" = per circuit = per user tab.

```csharp
public class ThemeService : IThemeService
{
    public Theme CurrentTheme { get; private set; } = Theme.System;
    public string AccentColor { get; private set; } = "#0078d4";
    public event Action? OnChange;

    public void SetTheme(Theme theme) { CurrentTheme = theme; OnChange?.Invoke(); }
    public void SetAccentColor(string color) { AccentColor = color; OnChange?.Invoke(); }
}
```

### 3. Components subscribe to changes

```razor
@implements IDisposable
@inject IThemeService Theme

<!-- render using Theme.CurrentTheme / Theme.AccentColor -->

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => Theme.OnChange += StateHasChanged;
    public void Dispose() => Theme.OnChange -= StateHasChanged;
}
```

### Why this works for all your requirements:

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| Any component reads/writes | All inject the same scoped service |
| Cross-component reactivity | `OnChange` event → `StateHasChanged` |
| Static layout updates | Header indicator is an interactive island |
| Per-user isolation | Scoped = per circuit |
| Persists across enhanced nav | Circuit (and its scoped services) survives enhanced navigation |

### Key insight

You don't need a `CascadingValue` or global state. The **scoped DI lifetime in Interactive Server already gives you per-circuit singleton behavior**. The only trick is ensuring components that must react (like the header indicator) are themselves interactive — even if the layout wrapping them is static.
